[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 7:53] I don't have margin by product. Pulling this together, what's your recommendation to the CEO?

[candidate · 9:23] My recommendation: Brew & Bean should raise menu prices, roughly 8-10%, phased in, and run a procurement reset on non-bean inputs in parallel. That gets margin back toward the mid-teens.

The reasoning: the entire 18-point margin decline is COGS, which went 42 to 58 points of revenue. Labor was flat at 22 and overhead moved only 2 points. That COGS rise is fully explained by input inflation — 40% on beans, 37.5% on everything else — and prices haven't moved in two years, so we've absorbed all of it. Revenue growth came from volume and bigger baskets, not pricing.

Math: at a 10% increase with flat volume, profit goes from 6 to 16 on 110 of revenue, about 15%.

Risks: volume loss if demand is more elastic than expected, and we don't have competitor pricing.

Next steps: price-test in a few markets, open dairy and packaging negotiations, and get margin by product to guide mix.
